This repository contains the server-side materials of SharePi: the backend
service, its container build, and the Terraform configuration that sets it up.
The source is published so that anyone who runs it with their own data can
read exactly what it does. It is not open source. Only the rights listed in
section 1 are granted; every other right is reserved.

1. What you may do

   a. Read, study and audit the source code and documentation.
   b. Deploy the official, unmodified release (the container image published
      by the copyright holder and the Terraform configuration in this
      repository) to your own Google Cloud project, and operate it for your
      own use and for the groups you invite to it.
   c. Set the input variables and files that the Terraform configuration
      exposes for that purpose (for example project_id, region,
      admin_emails). Doing so is not a modification.

2. What you may not do

   a. Modify, translate, adapt or create derivative works of the source code,
      the Terraform configuration or the container image.
   b. Copy, redistribute, publish, sublicense, sell or lease any part of
      them, except for the copies that your use under section 1 necessarily
      makes (including the copies that GitHub's own terms allow other users to
      make of a public repository).
   c. Offer the software, or a service built on it, to third parties as a
      hosted or managed product.
   d. Remove or alter this notice or any copyright notice.

3. Third-party components

   The software uses third-party components (for example Go modules and
   Terraform providers). They remain under their own licenses, which are not
   changed by this one.

